==> docker compose -f services.docker-compose.yml up
Creates and starts all containers defined in the services.docker-compose.yml file, using the specified configuration.
This command will run in the foreground and display logs from all containers.

==> docker build -t promptforge-proxy:latest .
Creates a Docker image named "promptforge-proxy" with the "latest" tag using the Dockerfile in the current directory.

==> docker build -t promptforge-proxy:latest -f proxy/Dockerfile proxy/
Creates a Docker image named "promptforge-proxy" with the "latest" tag using the Dockerfile located in the "proxy" directory.

==> kind load docker-image promptforge-proxy:latest --name promptforge-ai
Loads the Docker image "promptforge-proxy:latest" into the Kind cluster named "promptforge-ai".
